  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "What are the dimensions of $HK$, if $H$ is a $3\\times 7$ matrix and $K$ is a $7\\times 5$ matrix?",
  "worked_solution": "There are $7$ columns in $H$ and $7$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $H$ equals the number of rows in $K,$ the matrices $H$ and $K$ are conformable for multiplication, and $HK$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{H}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{7}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{K}_{\\boxed{\\text{7}}\\times 5}={HK}_{3\\times 5}\n$$",
